{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-20505" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y+6z=5 \\\\  & y-10z=-11 \\\\  & 4x+8y+13z=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20505" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 13 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 13 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -11 & -11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{11}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20505" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f9d1f89b8a7f3986d789bfa743b4fd8bbd59f6801acf717a3a5d11f579002872"} {"question" "q-20505" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20505" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20505" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y+z=-4 \\\\  & 2x+5y+3z=-10 \\\\  & 3x+6y+4z=-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 3 & -10 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 & -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 3 & -10 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f9d1f89b8a7f3986d789bfa743b4fd8bbd59f6801acf717a3a5d11f579002872"} {"question" "q-20515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20515" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20524" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 6 & 21\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20524" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 6 & 21\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20524" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f9d1f89b8a7f3986d789bfa743b4fd8bbd59f6801acf717a3a5d11f579002872"} {"question" "q-20524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f9d1f89b8a7f3986d789bfa743b4fd8bbd59f6801acf717a3a5d11f579002872"} {"question" "q-20508" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20508" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20508" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+2z=-3 \\\\  & x+2y+2z=2 \\\\  & 3x+4y+4z=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and hence solve the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+2z=-3 \\\\  & y=5 \\\\  & z=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. Substituting both $y=5$ and $z=-6$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+5+2(-6)=-3\\,⟹\\,x-7=-3\\,⟹\\,x=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=4,$ $y=5,$ and $z=-6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f9d1f89b8a7f3986d789bfa743b4fd8bbd59f6801acf717a3a5d11f579002872"} {"question" "q-20542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$x=-1,y=4$ and $z=-2$"] ["text" "$x=-11,y=4$ and $z=4$"] ["text" "$x=-2,y=4$ and $z=2$"] ["text" "$x=13,y=-4$ and $z=-4$"] ["text" "$x=4,y=5$ and $z=-6$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-20542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x=4,y=5$ and $z=-6$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-73580" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 20 & -10 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-73580" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & 20 & -10 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $\\frac{1}{3}$ and the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-73580" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f9d1f89b8a7f3986d789bfa743b4fd8bbd59f6801acf717a3a5d11f579002872"} {"question" "q-73580" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-73580" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -9 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-73580" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-73579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & -3x+6y-3z=18 \\\\  & -4x+8y-3z=2 \\\\  & y-4z=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-73579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 6 & -3 & 18 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 6 & -3 & 18 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -22\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+z=-6 \\\\ y-4z=-3 \\\\ z=-22,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=-22$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-4(-22)=-3\\,⟹\\,y=-91.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-91$ and $z=-22$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-2(-91)+(-22)=-6\\,⟹\\,x=-166.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-166$, $y=-91$, and $z=-22.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-73579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f9d1f89b8a7f3986d789bfa743b4fd8bbd59f6801acf717a3a5d11f579002872"} {"question" "q-73579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-73579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$x=-166$, $y=-91$, and $z=-22$"] ["text" "$x=-33$, $y=-15$, and $z=-3$"] ["text" "$x=-89$, $y=-47$, and $z=-11$"] ["text" "$x=142$, $y=85$, and $z=22$"] ["text" "$x=9$, $y=9$, and $z=3$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-73579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x=-166$, $y=-91$, and $z=-22$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-130927" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y-z=4 \\\\  & -3x-6y+4z=-8 \\\\  & 3x+7y-z=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-130927" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z=4 \\\\ y+2z=-2 \\\\ z=4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=4$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+2(4)=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-10$ and $z=4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2(-10)-(4)=4\\,⟹\\,x=28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-130927" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f9d1f89b8a7f3986d789bfa743b4fd8bbd59f6801acf717a3a5d11f579002872"} {"question" "q-130927" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-130927" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$x=-12$, $y=-10$, and $z=2$"] ["text" "$x=-12$, $y=6$, and $z=-4$"] ["text" "$x=18$, $y=6$, and $z=2$"] ["text" "$x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4$"] ["text" "$x=28$, $y=-6$, and $z=4$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-130927" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-73396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-y+2z=8 \\\\  & -2x+2y-3z=-11 \\\\  & x+z=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-73396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z=8 \\\\ y-z=1 \\\\ z=5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=5$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(5)=1\\,⟹\\,y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=6$ and $z=5$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(6)+2(5)=8\\,⟹\\,x=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=4$, $y=6$, and $z=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-73396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f9d1f89b8a7f3986d789bfa743b4fd8bbd59f6801acf717a3a5d11f579002872"} {"question" "q-73396" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-73396" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$x=-1$, $y=2$, and $z=5$"] ["text" "$x=1$, $y=-6$, and $z=-5$"] ["text" "$x=4$, $y=-5$, and $z=2$"] ["text" "$x=4$, $y=5$, and $z=2$"] ["text" "$x=4$, $y=6$, and $z=5$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-73396" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x=4$, $y=6$, and $z=5$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-73584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-73584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y-2z=3 \\\\ y+5z=-8 \\\\ z=4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=4$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+5(4)=-8\\,⟹\\,y=-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-28$ and $z=4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(-28)-2(4)=3\\,⟹\\,x=39.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=39$, $y=-28$, and $z=4.$ Or, in vector form $⟨39,-28,4⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-73584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f9d1f89b8a7f3986d789bfa743b4fd8bbd59f6801acf717a3a5d11f579002872"} {"question" "q-73584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-73584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-17,12,-4⟩"] ["math" "⟨-3,2,-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨11,-8,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨25,-18,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨39,-28,4⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "q-73584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨39,-28,4⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4439dbe62cc33e8bf0733fd09a9c77390fec505c15830537178cac38d88c9b0"} {"question" "e-4701" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=1 \\\\ y+z=-2 \\\\ -x+2y+z=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/example-4701.json" "file_sha256" "84dfcca7e7bd089bb76913283a83665b63a2565877e395f0e4da98025952e3b3"} {"question" "e-4701" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=1 \\\\ y+z=-2 \\\\ z=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=2$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+(2)=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=-4$ and $z=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(-4)+(2)=1\\,⟹\\,x=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-5,$ $y=-4,$ and $z=2.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -5,-4,2 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/example-4701.json" "file_sha256" "84dfcca7e7bd089bb76913283a83665b63a2565877e395f0e4da98025952e3b3"} {"question" "e-4702" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x+y+z=-2 \\\\  & x+y+2z=-1 \\\\  & x+2y+z=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/example-4702.json" "file_sha256" "f0fc86bccf69156c5068b94de129837b9e62a8846dc17d8af13d98f6b7980696"} {"question" "e-4702" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get $a_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+z=-2 \\\\ y=3 \\\\ z=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z,$ and the second equation $y=3$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting these values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(3)+(1)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-6,$ $y=3,$ and $z=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -6,3,1 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/example-4702.json" "file_sha256" "f0fc86bccf69156c5068b94de129837b9e62a8846dc17d8af13d98f6b7980696"} {"question" "q-20505" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "d2a23e81810a7b961785718c1b37f8b21b481825e2fffa99cd4335ecbe83e03b" "reviewer_session" "01a118cc-89a0-7c90-9221-d6599ae13bca" "rationale" "The original augmented matrix has rows [1,2,6,5], [0,1,-10,-11], and [4,8,13,9]. Applying R3:=R3-4R1 gives [0,0,-11,-11]; multiplying R3 by -1/11 gives [0,0,1,1]. The first two rows remain unchanged, yielding exactly original option 4. The stored matrix has identical entries. This is a source-backed derived judgment corroborated by the authentic worked solution and saved Correct grade." "bindings" {"problem" "ba2585768d9d602ff43bb93c902b23425dd03871b829790275bac2ecc4a214ad" "worked_solution" "82074f23b296c321eca01826fc75d74e2f164afec21a738b6e735ca0e4207d7a" "original_field" "1e83bcfefe1ddf61e31cef4e27fe86bdd69d964370767c57087d598c428bc354" "reviewed_field" "f53870a699e3eba31905565fd23dc0b9bfb7752c5777241ab783a65f05e36857" "raw_widget" "57f4af61e081c915c5f3cfc893116ba5aba02e81e9a99686c014157c5d06b517"} "evidence_files" [{"path" "q-20505-before.png" "sha256" "14c4be39ea6ec97da7c92757eb817e183937145556412808b8e42ebfaece7b8a"} {"path" "q-20505-after.json" "sha256" "d85eca6bfe0e17335c0c965f243dc5fd52d2d789fe7369583b3a0e0b143f6b7b"} {"path" "history-q-20505.png" "sha256" "4a609f6b21cbfc6bd6087260016f33155e0a1abffb0769bd6baa503dcec2c7cc"}]} {"question" "q-20505" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "reviewed_ma_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040313/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "d2a23e81810a7b961785718c1b37f8b21b481825e2fffa99cd4335ecbe83e03b" "rationale" "The original augmented matrix has rows [1,2,6,5], [0,1,-10,-11], and [4,8,13,9]. Applying R3:=R3-4R1 gives [0,0,-11,-11]; multiplying R3 by -1/11 gives [0,0,1,1]. The first two rows remain unchanged, yielding exactly original option 4. The stored matrix has identical entries. This is a source-backed derived judgment corroborated by the authentic worked solution and saved Correct grade."}] "usage" {"q-73396" [] "e-4702" [] "e-4701" [] "q-20505" []} "basis" 1429 "retractions" [[17592186097101 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n${x + 2y + 6z = 5; y - 10z =-11; 4x + 8y + 13z = 9$\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form."] [17592186097101 :question/answer-fields 17592186095012] [17592186097269 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n${x - y + 2z = 8; - 2x + 2y - 3z =-11; x + z = 9$.\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [17592186096382 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$x - y + z = 1; y + z =-2; - x + 2y + z =-1$.\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [17592186096382 :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nM\\begin{vmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{3} + R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{3} \\mid:=R_{3} + (-1)R_{2}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\nx - y + z = 1; y + z =-2; z = 2\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=2$ tells us the value of $z$. Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny + (2) =-2⟹y =-4\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=-4$ and $z=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx - (-4) + (2) = 1⟹x =-5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-5$, $y=-4$, and $z=2$. Or, in vector form, $\\langle -5,-4,2 \\rangle$."] [17592186096383 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n$x + y + z =-2; x + y + 2z =-1; x + 2y + z = 1$.\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [17592186096383 :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nM\\begin{vmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & R_{2}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{2} + (-1)R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{3} \\mid:=R_{3} + (-1)R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNote that we get $a_{22}=0$. Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n$M\\begin{vmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & R_{2}\\end{vmatrix}↔R_{3}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\nx + y + z =-2; y = 3; z = 1\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z$, and the second equation $y=3$ tells us the value of $y$. Substituting these values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx + (3) + (1) =-2⟹x =-6\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-6$, $y=3$, and $z=1$. Or, in vector form, $\\langle -6,3,1 \\rangle$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186095013 17592186095014 17592186095015 17592186095016 17592186095017 17592186095972 17592186095973 17592186095974 17592186095975 17592186095976] "immutable_fields" [[17592186095012 :answer-field/correct] [17592186095012 :answer-field/id] [17592186095012 :answer-field/key] [17592186095012 :answer-field/type] [17592186095971 :answer-field/correct] [17592186095971 :answer-field/id] [17592186095971 :answer-field/key] [17592186095971 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
